course: dictionary
lesson: 6114
title: Microchip: a tiny chip with a big job
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one. «A microchip is a tiny chip under a pet's skin» is about animals, but «Most microchips carry a 15-digit number» could be about pets or computers. Look for clues like under a pet's skin, silicon or circuits.
explain: Context also tells you what kind of word you are reading. «To microchip a pet means to put this chip in» uses microchip as a doing word. Test it by swapping in a different word: «The vet will ___ the puppy today» works, so microchip is a verb here.
explain: «In the late 1950s engineers invented the microchip, which put many tiny parts onto a small piece of silicon.» Invented, tiny parts and silicon are the clues. A microchip is a small piece that holds many tiny parts, not a plain potato crisp or a bag of rice.
fact: A microchip is a very small piece of material, usually silicon, with tiny electronic circuits on it.
fact: Inside computers and phones, microchips store information and do calculations.
fact: A pet microchip is about the size of a grain of rice and is put under the skin by a vet.
fact: «Microchip» can be a noun (a microchip) or a verb (to microchip a pet, meaning to put a chip in it).
fact: Microchips are also called chips or integrated circuits, like the «computer chip» in a laptop.
exercise: «A microchip is about the size of a grain of rice and is placed under the skin between the shoulder blades.» Where is a pet's microchip placed? | *Under the skin between the shoulder blades | In the food bowl | On the collar | In the tail
exercise: What material is a microchip usually made from? | Paper | Wood | Cotton | *Silicon
exercise: «The vet will microchip the puppy today.» What kind of word is microchip in this sentence? | A place | A colour | *A doing word (verb) | A thing only (noun)
test: «Most microchips carry a 15-digit number that no other animal shares.» Why does a pet need a number on its microchip? | *So a lost pet can be identified and returned | To keep it warm | To make it run faster | To tell the time
test: «The chip has no battery, lasts for life, and cannot track a pet like a GPS tracker.» What does this tell you? | It must be replaced each year | It shows the pet's location on a map | It needs charging every night | *It cannot show where a pet is
exam: In a computer, what does a microchip do? | Plays music only | Makes the keyboard waterproof | Keeps the food cold | *Stores information and does calculations
